IMPORT prelude

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 (Singapore) -- ss 8 to 16, s 24, s 34B,
-- and First Schedule paragraph 5.
--
-- The rest of the operative Act, after s 7 and the compensation tables. Three
-- groups: what counts as an accident arising out of and in the course of the
-- employment beyond s 7(1) (ss 8, 9), when a disease is treated as a work
-- injury (s 10), and who else may be made to pay (s 13), plus the medical
-- treatment liability (s 16 with First Schedule paragraph 5), the duty to
-- insure (s 24) and the Part 3A substitution for platform workers (s 34B).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the claims procedure in Part 4, the designated-insurer regime in
-- Part 3 Division 2, appeals, and ss 34D to 34N individually -- those are the
-- platform-worker counterparts of sections already encoded, and s 34B is what
-- maps them.

§ `Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 -- liability beyond section 7`

§§ `8 -- Accidents deemed to be in the course of employment`

-- s 8 adds three deeming rules to s 7(1). Each one makes an accident count that
-- would otherwise be arguable.
--
-- s 8(1): TRAVELLING AS A PASSENGER. The accident happens while the employee is
-- "(WITH THE EXPRESS OR IMPLIED PERMISSION OF THE EMPLOYER) travelling as a
-- passenger by any means of transport to or from the employee's workplace",
-- AND at the time the transport (i) "is operated by or on behalf of the
-- employer, or by some other person who operates [it] pursuant to arrangements
-- made with the employer"; and (ii) "IS NOT OPERATED IN THE ORDINARY COURSE OF
-- A PUBLIC TRANSPORT SERVICE."
--
-- So the company bus is covered and the public bus is not, however the journey
-- was arranged.
DECLARE TravelFacts HAS
    `travelling as a passenger to or from the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with the express or implied permission of the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transport is operated by or on behalf of the employer, or under arrangements made with the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transport is operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the travel` IS A TravelFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8(1) deems the accident to arise out of and in the course of employment` IF
        `the travel`'s `travelling as a passenger to or from the workplace`
    AND `the travel`'s `with the express or implied permission of the employer`
    AND `the travel`'s `the transport is operated by or on behalf of the employer, or under arrangements made with the employer`
    AND NOT `the travel`'s `the transport is operated in the ordinary course of a public transport service`

-- s 8(2): EMERGENCY AT THE WORKPLACE. The accident happens "in or about the
-- employee's workplace" while the employee is taking steps, "on an ACTUAL OR
-- SUPPOSED emergency", to rescue or protect a person "who is, OR IS THOUGHT TO
-- BE OR POSSIBLY TO BE, injured or imperilled", or to avert or minimise damage
-- to or loss of property.
--
-- "Actual or supposed", and "thought to be or possibly to be": the employee who
-- runs towards a fire that turns out to be a false alarm is covered.
DECLARE EmergencyFacts HAS
    `the accident happened in or about the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was an actual or supposed emergency at the workplace` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was acting to rescue or protect a person injured or imperilled, or thought to be` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was acting to avert or minimise damage to or loss of property` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN EmergencyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8(2) deems the accident to arise out of and in the course of employment` IF
        `the facts`'s `the accident happened in or about the workplace`
    AND `the facts`'s `there was an actual or supposed emergency at the workplace`
    AND `the employee was taking one of the two kinds of step` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN EmergencyFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee was taking one of the two kinds of step` IF
        `the facts`'s `the employee was acting to rescue or protect a person injured or imperilled, or thought to be`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the employee was acting to avert or minimise damage to or loss of property`

-- s 8(3): BREAKING THE RULES. Despite the employee acting (a) in contravention
-- of written law, regulations or the employer's orders, or (b) without
-- instructions, the accident is still deemed to arise out of and in the course
-- of the employment if (c) it would have done so had the employee not been so
-- acting, AND (d) "that act was done FOR THE PURPOSES OF AND IN CONNECTION WITH
-- the employer's trade or business."
--
-- Disobedience does not defeat the claim; acting outside the employer's
-- business does.
DECLARE DisobedienceFacts HAS
    `the employee was acting in contravention of law, regulations or the employer's orders` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
    `the employee was acting without instructions from the employer` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
    `it would have arisen out of and in the course of the employment had the employee not been so acting` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
    `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DisobedienceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 8(3) deems the accident to arise out of and in the course of employment` IF
        `the employee was acting in one of the two ways section 8(3) names` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `it would have arisen out of and in the course of the employment had the employee not been so acting`
    AND `the facts`'s `the act was done for the purposes of and in connection with the employer's trade or business`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DisobedienceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee was acting in one of the two ways section 8(3) names` IF
        `the facts`'s `the employee was acting in contravention of law, regulations or the employer's orders`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the employee was acting without instructions from the employer`

§§ `9 -- Accidents outside Singapore`

-- s 9: the Act extends to an accident outside Singapore where the employee is
-- "(a) ORDINARILY RESIDENT in Singapore; AND (b) EMPLOYED BY AN EMPLOYER IN
-- SINGAPORE but is REQUIRED IN THE COURSE OF THE EMPLOYEE'S EMPLOYMENT to work
-- outside Singapore."
--
-- All three elements, and the third matters: an employee who goes abroad by
-- choice rather than requirement is outside s 9.
GIVEN `ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `employed by an employer in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `required in the course of the employment to work outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act extends to the accident outside Singapore` IF
        `ordinarily resident in Singapore`
    AND `employed by an employer in Singapore`
    AND `required in the course of the employment to work outside Singapore`

§§ `10 -- Diseases treated as work injuries`

-- s 10(1): where incapacity or death results from a disease contracted in one
-- of three circumstances, "compensation is payable AS IF THE DISEASE WERE A
-- WORK INJURY":
--   (a) the employee contracts a SCHEDULED occupational disease WHILE employed
--       in the occupation specified for it in the Second Schedule;
--   (b) the employee contracts it AFTER CEASING that employment, but WITHIN THE
--       LIMITATION PERIOD for that disease (the Second Schedule's third column);
--   (c) on or after 1 June 2012, the employee contracts a disease NOT in the
--       Second Schedule that is "DIRECTLY ATTRIBUTABLE TO AN EXPOSURE TO A
--       CHEMICAL OR BIOLOGICAL AGENT" arising out of and in the course of the
--       employment.
--
-- Limb (c) is the open-ended one, and it is narrower than it looks: a chemical
-- or biological agent only. A disease caused by noise, vibration, radiation or
-- repetitive strain is outside it unless the Second Schedule lists it.
DECLARE DiseaseFacts HAS
    `incapacity or death resulted from the disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (a) and (b)
    `the disease is specified in the Second Schedule for the employee's occupation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee was employed in that occupation when the disease was contracted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee had ceased that employment when the disease was contracted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was contracted within the limitation period specified for that disease` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- (c)
    `contracted on or after 1 June 2012`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `directly attributable to an exposure to a chemical or biological agent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that exposure arose out of and in the course of the employment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DiseaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (a) of section 10(1) applies` IF
        `the facts`'s `the disease is specified in the Second Schedule for the employee's occupation`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employee was employed in that occupation when the disease was contracted`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DiseaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (b) of section 10(1) applies` IF
        `the facts`'s `the disease is specified in the Second Schedule for the employee's occupation`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employee had ceased that employment when the disease was contracted`
    AND `the facts`'s `it was contracted within the limitation period specified for that disease`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DiseaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `limb (c) of section 10(1) applies` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `the disease is specified in the Second Schedule for the employee's occupation`
    AND `the facts`'s `contracted on or after 1 June 2012`
    AND `the facts`'s `directly attributable to an exposure to a chemical or biological agent`
    AND `the facts`'s `that exposure arose out of and in the course of the employment`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DiseaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disease is compensable as if it were a work injury` IF
        `the facts`'s `incapacity or death resulted from the disease`
    AND `a limb of section 10(1) applies` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A DiseaseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a limb of section 10(1) applies` IF
        `limb (a) of section 10(1) applies` `the facts`
    ..  `limb (b) of section 10(1) applies` `the facts`
    OR  `limb (c) of section 10(1) applies` `the facts`

§§ `13 -- The principal may be directed to pay`

-- s 13(1): where a principal contracts, in the course of or for the purpose of
-- its trade or business, with a contractor for the execution of work or the
-- supply of labour, "THE COMMISSIONER MAY DIRECT the principal to fulfil the
-- obligations of the employer under this Act in relation to any employee of the
-- contractor employed in the execution of the work".
--
-- Note the difference from s 65 of the Motor Vehicles Act, which makes the
-- principal jointly and severally liable BY OPERATION OF LAW. Here nothing
-- happens unless the Commissioner directs it, so the injured employee depends
-- on an official decision rather than on a right.
--
-- s 13(2): on a direction, compensation is calculated "with reference to the
-- EARNINGS OF THE EMPLOYEE UNDER THE CONTRACTOR", not the principal's.
-- s 13(3): the principal who pays is entitled to be indemnified by the employer.
DECLARE PrincipalFacts HAS
    `the principal contracted in the course of or for the purpose of its trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract was for the execution of work or the supply of labour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is an employee of the contractor employed in the execution of the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner has directed the principal under section 13(1)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PrincipalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may direct the principal` IF
        `the facts`'s `the principal contracted in the course of or for the purpose of its trade or business`
    AND `the facts`'s `the contract was for the execution of work or the supply of labour`
    AND `the facts`'s `the employee is an employee of the contractor employed in the execution of the work`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PrincipalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is liable to pay the employee` IF
        `the Commissioner may direct the principal` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `the Commissioner has directed the principal under section 13(1)`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A PrincipalFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal is entitled to be indemnified by the employer` IF
    `the principal is liable to pay the employee` `the facts`

§§ `16 with First Schedule paragraph 5 -- Medical treatment`

-- First Schedule paragraph 5(1): the compensation for medical treatment is
-- "THE LOWER of the following amounts --
--   (a) the cost of medical treatment received by the employee WITHIN A PERIOD
--       OF ONE YEAR AFTER THE DATE OF THE ACCIDENT causing the injury;
--   (b) ... $45,000 [before 1 November 2025] or $53,000 [on or after]."
--
-- TWO CEILINGS, and the first is temporal. Treatment in the thirteenth month
-- counts for nothing, however necessary, and however far below the money cap
-- the employee is.
`the medical treatment cap before 1 November 2025` MEANS 45000
`the medical treatment cap on or after 1 November 2025` MEANS 53000

DECLARE MedicalTreatment HAS
    `the treatment was by a health professional or at an approved medical institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an attending health professional certified it to be necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cost of treatment received within one year after the date of the accident` IS A NUMBER
    `the cost of treatment received after that year`  IS A NUMBER
    `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 16(1)(b): the section 9 employee treated abroad.
    `the employee is one mentioned in section 9`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the treatment was received outside Singapore for an accident occurring outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is of the opinion it was required immediately due to the nature of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A MedicalTreatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment is within section 16(1)(a)` IF
        `the treatment`'s `the treatment was by a health professional or at an approved medical institution`
    AND `the treatment`'s `an attending health professional certified it to be necessary`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A MedicalTreatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the treatment is within section 16(1)(b)` IF
        `the treatment`'s `the employee is one mentioned in section 9`
    AND `the treatment`'s `the treatment was received outside Singapore for an accident occurring outside Singapore`
    AND `the treatment`'s `the Commissioner is of the opinion it was required immediately due to the nature of the injury`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A MedicalTreatment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is liable for the medical treatment` IF
        `the treatment is within section 16(1)(a)` `the treatment`
    OR  `the treatment is within section 16(1)(b)` `the treatment`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A MedicalTreatment
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the medical treatment money cap` IS
    IF   `the treatment`'s `the accident took place on or after 1 November 2025`
    THEN `the medical treatment cap on or after 1 November 2025`
    ELSE `the medical treatment cap before 1 November 2025`

GIVEN `the treatment` IS A MedicalTreatment
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the compensation for medical treatment` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the employer is liable for the medical treatment` `the treatment` THEN 0
        IF `the treatment`'s `the cost of treatment received within one year after the date of the accident`
               GREATER THAN `the medical treatment money cap` `the treatment`
            THEN `the medical treatment money cap` `the treatment`
        OTHERWISE `the treatment`'s `the cost of treatment received within one year after the date of the accident`

§§ `24 -- The duty to insure`

-- s 24(1): "EVERY employer MUST insure and maintain insurance under one or more
-- approved employee insurance policies with one or more designated employer's
-- insurers against ALL LIABILITIES that the employer may incur under this Act
-- in respect of EVERY EMPLOYEE of the employer."
--
-- s 24(2): it does not apply to "the EXCLUDED CLASSES of employees prescribed",
-- and applies "subject to any MINIMUM PRESCRIBED AMOUNT". Both are prescribed
-- and were not retrieved.
DECLARE InsuranceFacts HAS
    `the employer has insured and maintained insurance under an approved policy with a designated insurer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee is of an excluded class prescribed for section 24(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount insured meets any minimum prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN InsuranceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 24(1) applies in respect of this employee` IF
    NOT `the facts`'s `the employee is of an excluded class prescribed for section 24(2)(a)`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN InsuranceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer contravenes section 24(1)` IF
        `section 24(1) applies in respect of this employee` `the facts`
    AND `the insurance is absent or insufficient` `the facts`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN InsuranceFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the insurance is absent or insufficient` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `the employer has insured and maintained insurance under an approved policy with a designated insurer`
    OR  NOT `the facts`'s `the amount insured meets any minimum prescribed amount`

§§ `34B -- How Part 2 applies to a platform worker`

-- s 34B(a): Part 2 applies to a platform operator and platform worker as it
-- does to an employer and employee, with the sections in the second column
-- applying IN LIEU of those in the first:
--
--     replaced   applicable
--        7    ->    34D
--        8    ->    34F
--       10    ->    34G
--       11    ->    34H
--       12    ->    34I
--       14    ->    34K
--       15    ->    34L
--       16    ->    34M
--       17    ->    34N
--
-- THE DEPOSITED WICA2019.txt GETS THIS TABLE WRONG, in the same way it gets
-- Tables A and B wrong: the applicable sections are shifted up one row against
-- the replaced sections, so the text reads "8 -> 34D" where the PDF has
-- "7 -> 34D" and "8 -> 34F". The mapping below is taken from the PDF. See
-- NOTES.md.
DECLARE ReplacedSection IS ONE OF
    `section 7`
    `section 8`
    `section 10`
    `section 11`
    `section 12`
    `section 14`
    `section 15`
    `section 16`
    `section 17`
    `a section Part 3A does not replace`

GIVEN `the section` IS A ReplacedSection
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the section that applies to a platform worker instead` IS
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `section 7`  THEN "34D"
    WHEN `section 8`  THEN "34F"
    WHEN `section 10` THEN "34G"
    WHEN `section 11` THEN "34H"
    WHEN `section 12` THEN "34I"
    WHEN `section 14` THEN "34K"
    WHEN `section 15` THEN "34L"
    WHEN `section 16` THEN "34M"
    WHEN `section 17` THEN "34N"
    OTHERWISE "the section itself, unmodified"

GIVEN `the section` IS A ReplacedSection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3A replaces this section for a platform worker` IF
    CONSIDER `the section`
    WHEN `a section Part 3A does not replace` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
